From d4c8eebd8690c3b46d50791603ce6f69829f3dc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:47:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: each machine's HUD, track objects and finish fade
 follow its seat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gibax (2026-11-26): "le joueur a que son écran du perso sur sa console ...
tout indiqué SON joueur et aucun autre". A 2-player race, Sonic (seat 0) to
the AI, Knuckles (seat 1) still at the start, showed on Knuckles's screen:
- Sonic's route icon and stick prompt: a block of the 1P HUD task drawn for
  racer 0 written in the code (0x8041EE00, r22); now the seat's racer. The
  same for the task 0x804250C0 (0x8042653C, r20; no visible change seen);
- the start gate and its 15 m / 30 m boards only once Sonic came near: the
  objects' drawing compares each object's zone with racer 0's (0x80612BD8,
  and its flags +0xBA8), alone or in a loop over the views; 215 sites listed
  from the REL's disassembly (work/phase2/zones_objets.py) now use the seat's;
- the time, rank and speed fading out at Sonic's finish: the task 0x804306F0
  fades them once racer 0 has crossed the line (0x804309C4); now the seat's.

And a desync, older than this: the racers left out of the 1P drawing by
their zone also skipped their animation (0x8040B630, b past it); since the
zone of reference is the seat's, racer 6 crossing the line near Knuckles
moved on one more animation frame on his machine (+0x760 0x4C against 0x4B,
then +0x8D4 for good). That branch now goes to the animation too.

The racers' sound handles (+0xF44-0xF4B, +0xF50-0xF5F: only the sound
functions use them) leave the checksum: they follow the order sounds start
in, which differs once objects sound around each machine's seat.

Measured (SRNP_PAUSE_JEU photos, same race): Knuckles sees the gate from the
start, no prompt of Sonic's, his time/rank/speed after Sonic's finish;
Sonic's screen unchanged; 89 identical checksums, 0 divergences (8 before,
the animation); the mirrored race (Sonic still, Knuckles to the AI): 83
identical, 0 divergences, Knuckles's tricks and rings on his screen only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
